From: Carlos Fundora <carlosfundora@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 16:06:34 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] rayon-core: opt-in batch stealing and steal groups

Add two opt-in scheduler options. Their defaults keep upstream behavior.

- ThreadPoolBuilder::steal_batch_limit(k): an idle worker moves up to k
  jobs per steal from a victim deque or the global injector
  (crossbeam-deque steal_batch_with_limit_and_pop). Batching applies only
  at the top of the thief's stack. A worker waiting inside a running job
  keeps single-item stealing, so stolen subtrees cannot pile up on its
  stack. Unrestricted batching overflowed worker stacks in rayon's suite.
  The thief runs the oldest stolen job, as upstream single-item stealing
  does. Crossbeam returns the youngest job of a batch taken from a LIFO
  deque, so it is pushed back and the oldest is taken from the front of
  the thief's own deque. find_any short-circuiting depends on this order.
  Extra moved jobs are announced to the sleep counters. Broadcast jobs
  are never batched.
- ThreadPoolBuilder::steal_groups(groups): a validated partition of
  thread indices. steal() scans victims in the thief's own group first,
  then the rest, so the set of victims scanned is unchanged.
- Environment fallbacks RAYON_STEAL_BATCH_LIMIT=<k> and
  RAYON_STEAL_GROUPS=contiguous:<n> apply only when the builder option is
  unset. ErrorKind::InvalidStealGroups reports bad partitions.

Tests cover result preservation, idle sleep, partition validation, nested
stack depth on 256 KiB stacks at batch 32, and oldest-job execution. The
last test runs indefinitely without the fix. rayon-core passes 145/145
with defaults and with RAYON_STEAL_BATCH_LIMIT=8
RAYON_STEAL_GROUPS=contiguous:2. rayon passes 596/596 with defaults, with
that environment, and with RAYON_STEAL_BATCH_LIMIT=32.

